1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:04,004
There are only four ways to lose
points on SAT transition questions.

2
00:00:04,968 --> 00:00:07,147
Two choices that do the same job.

3
00:00:07,218 --> 00:00:09,182
A however that should be a therefore.

4
00:00:10,146 --> 00:00:13,182
A contrast word you grabbed because
there was a contrast somewhere else.

5
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:15,805
And the fourth one looks completely right,

6
00:00:15,825 --> 00:00:17,683
because it really is a contrast word.

7
00:00:17,754 --> 00:00:19,718
The first three are quick to fix.

8
00:00:19,932 --> 00:00:23,770
The fourth is in contrast when
only one thing is being described.

9
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:25,948
That's question seven, the hardest one,

10
00:00:25,968 --> 00:00:27,074
so stay for it.

11
00:00:27,397 --> 00:00:30,984
The method for all four: predict the
relationship before you look at the

12
00:00:31,004 --> 00:00:32,004
choices.

13
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,325
Seven questions, easy to hard.

14
00:00:34,352 --> 00:00:36,638
Keep score, and see if
you can get all seven.

15
00:00:36,697 --> 00:00:38,783
A transition doesn't add information.

16
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:41,054
It tells you how two ideas connect.

17
00:00:41,482 --> 00:00:44,605
So the real question is: what's the
relationship between the sentence before the

18
00:00:44,625 --> 00:00:46,625
blank and the sentence after it?

19
00:00:46,647 --> 00:00:48,147
There are seven to know.

20
00:00:48,576 --> 00:00:50,754
One: contrast.

21
00:00:51,504 --> 00:00:53,413
The next idea goes against the last one.

22
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:55,769
However, but, yet, in
contrast, by contrast,

23
00:00:55,789 --> 00:00:56,770
on the other hand.

24
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:59,361
Concession is a close cousin.

25
00:00:59,718 --> 00:01:02,091
Nevertheless, nonetheless, even so, still.

26
00:01:02,111 --> 00:01:04,469
It means: despite that.

27
00:01:04,517 --> 00:01:06,696
Two: cause and effect.

28
00:01:07,303 --> 00:01:09,339
The next idea is a result.

29
00:01:10,053 --> 00:01:12,997
Therefore, thus,
consequently, as a result,

30
00:01:13,017 --> 00:01:14,231
for this reason.

31
00:01:14,946 --> 00:01:17,160
Three: addition.

32
00:01:17,588 --> 00:01:19,767
More of the same kind of point.

33
00:01:20,446 --> 00:01:24,033
Moreover, furthermore,
additionally, in addition,

34
00:01:24,053 --> 00:01:25,053
also.

35
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:29,017
Similarly and likewise
add a parallel case.

36
00:01:29,105 --> 00:01:30,569
Four: example.

37
00:01:30,819 --> 00:01:34,192
The next sentence is a specific
case of a general claim.

38
00:01:34,212 --> 00:01:36,497
For example, for instance, to illustrate.

39
00:01:37,176 --> 00:01:39,334
Five: sequence or time.

40
00:01:39,354 --> 00:01:40,871
First, next, then, later, subsequently,

41
00:01:40,891 --> 00:01:42,140
meanwhile, finally.

42
00:01:42,214 --> 00:01:45,927
Six: emphasis or clarification.

43
00:01:46,285 --> 00:01:48,587
In fact and indeed push
the same idea further.

44
00:01:48,607 --> 00:01:51,249
In other words and that is
restate it more clearly.

45
00:01:52,142 --> 00:01:53,999
Seven: conclusion.

46
00:01:54,749 --> 00:01:58,464
In conclusion, in sum, in short, overall.

47
00:01:58,495 --> 00:02:00,690
You don't need to memorize every word.

48
00:02:00,710 --> 00:02:03,567
You need to know which
group each one belongs to,

49
00:02:03,602 --> 00:02:06,495
because the SAT is really
asking which group fits.

50
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:07,530
Here's the format.

51
00:02:09,637 --> 00:02:13,244
A short passage with a blank, often
at the start of the last sentence.

52
00:02:13,851 --> 00:02:16,867
The question says: which choice
completes the text with the most logical

53
00:02:16,887 --> 00:02:17,829
transition?

54
00:02:17,849 --> 00:02:22,206
To answer it, read the sentence before
the blank and the sentence after it.

55
00:02:22,671 --> 00:02:24,758
Sometimes you need the whole passage,

56
00:02:24,778 --> 00:02:27,778
because the last sentence can
connect back to an earlier one.

57
00:02:27,827 --> 00:02:30,720
And watch how fragile the logic is.

58
00:02:31,649 --> 00:02:33,399
The trail was steep.

59
00:02:33,676 --> 00:02:36,729
blank the hikers moved slowly.

60
00:02:36,764 --> 00:02:39,194
That's cause and effect: therefore.

61
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:41,027
Now change one word.

62
00:02:41,669 --> 00:02:43,456
The trail was steep.

63
00:02:43,563 --> 00:02:45,775
blank the hikers moved quickly.

64
00:02:45,795 --> 00:02:48,259
Now it's a surprise, so it's a contrast:

65
00:02:48,295 --> 00:02:49,097
however.

66
00:02:49,117 --> 00:02:53,117
Same sentences, one word different,
and the transition flips.

67
00:02:53,142 --> 00:02:54,535
So here's the method.

68
00:02:54,607 --> 00:02:56,230
Step one: cover the choices.

69
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:57,428
Don't look at them yet.

70
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:01,642
Step two: read the sentence before
the blank and the sentence after it.

71
00:03:01,690 --> 00:03:04,956
Step three: name the
relationship in a word or two.

72
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:05,976
Against?

73
00:03:06,011 --> 00:03:07,011
Result?

74
00:03:07,047 --> 00:03:08,206
More of the same?

75
00:03:08,226 --> 00:03:09,439
An example?

76
00:03:09,976 --> 00:03:11,583
Later in time?

77
00:03:12,369 --> 00:03:16,491
Step four: uncover the choices,
find the one from that group,

78
00:03:16,511 --> 00:03:19,833
and read the sentence with it
in place to make sure it works.

79
00:03:19,878 --> 00:03:20,914
Let's try it.

80
00:03:21,307 --> 00:03:25,144
Venus is sometimes called Earth's twin
because the two planets are similar in

81
00:03:25,164 --> 00:03:26,414
size and structure.

82
00:03:26,628 --> 00:03:30,181
blank the surface of Venus
is far hotter than Earth's:

83
00:03:30,252 --> 00:03:32,110
it is hot enough to melt lead.

84
00:03:32,167 --> 00:03:33,274
Pause and try it.

85
00:03:36,504 --> 00:03:39,611
Before the blank: Venus is like Earth.

86
00:03:40,003 --> 00:03:42,305
After it: Venus is very different.

87
00:03:42,325 --> 00:03:43,575
That's a contrast.

88
00:03:44,111 --> 00:03:46,039
Predict: however, or but.

89
00:03:46,647 --> 00:03:48,503
The answer is A, however.

90
00:03:48,578 --> 00:03:52,328
Similarly would mean
Venus is like Earth again.

91
00:03:52,936 --> 00:03:55,864
Therefore would mean being
Earth's twin causes the heat.

92
00:03:56,292 --> 00:03:59,415
And the heat isn't an example
of the two planets being alike,

93
00:03:59,435 --> 00:04:01,353
so for example doesn't work either.

94
00:04:01,373 --> 00:04:02,445
Question two.

95
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:07,210
Unlike most substances, water is less
dense in its solid form than in its liquid

96
00:04:07,230 --> 00:04:08,058
form.

97
00:04:08,078 --> 00:04:12,022
blank ice floats on the surface of lakes
and ponds instead of sinking to the

98
00:04:12,042 --> 00:04:12,731
bottom.

99
00:04:12,751 --> 00:04:13,858
Pause and try it.

100
00:04:17,088 --> 00:04:20,801
Before: solid water is less
dense than liquid water.

101
00:04:20,838 --> 00:04:22,409
After: ice floats.

102
00:04:23,195 --> 00:04:28,532
Things that are less dense float, so
the second sentence is the result of the

103
00:04:28,552 --> 00:04:29,552
first.

104
00:04:29,624 --> 00:04:32,088
Predict: therefore, or as a result.

105
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:33,109
That's D.

106
00:04:33,129 --> 00:04:35,022
Nevertheless is the trap.

107
00:04:35,343 --> 00:04:38,450
The phrase unlike most substances
sounds like a contrast.

108
00:04:38,772 --> 00:04:41,556
But that contrast is
inside the first sentence.

109
00:04:41,772 --> 00:04:44,592
Between the two sentences,
it's cause and effect.

110
00:04:44,806 --> 00:04:47,680
Nevertheless would mean ice
floats despite being less dense,

111
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:48,843
which is backwards.

112
00:04:48,918 --> 00:04:50,240
Question three.

113
00:04:50,632 --> 00:04:54,311
Some animals turn objects from
their surroundings into tools.

114
00:04:54,552 --> 00:04:58,068
blank New Caledonian crows
break twigs off bushes,

115
00:04:58,088 --> 00:05:02,588
trim them into sticks, and use the sticks
to pull insects out of holes in logs.

116
00:05:02,649 --> 00:05:03,756
Pause and try it.

117
00:05:06,986 --> 00:05:08,859
The first sentence is a general claim:

118
00:05:08,879 --> 00:05:10,681
some animals make tools.

119
00:05:10,701 --> 00:05:13,466
The second is one specific case: crows.

120
00:05:13,486 --> 00:05:19,894
General, then specific, means example.

121
00:05:19,914 --> 00:05:21,808
The answer is B, for instance.

122
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:23,899
In other words is the tempting one.

123
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:29,199
But in other words means the next
sentence says the same thing again.

124
00:05:29,219 --> 00:05:31,291
This one doesn't restate the claim.

125
00:05:31,898 --> 00:05:34,541
It adds a new, narrower case.

126
00:05:34,608 --> 00:05:35,680
Question four.

127
00:05:35,858 --> 00:05:39,767
The Svalbard Global Seed Vault, built
inside a mountain on a remote Arctic

128
00:05:39,787 --> 00:05:44,323
island, stores backup copies of seeds
from gene banks around the world.

129
00:05:44,537 --> 00:05:48,231
The vault sits well above sea level, so
it should stay dry even if sea levels

130
00:05:48,251 --> 00:05:49,251
rise.

131
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:53,025
blank the permafrost and thick rock
surrounding the vault would keep the seeds

132
00:05:53,045 --> 00:05:55,403
frozen even if the power failed.

133
00:05:55,425 --> 00:05:56,533
Pause and try it.

134
00:05:59,763 --> 00:06:03,620
Before the blank: one way
the vault protects the seeds.

135
00:06:04,334 --> 00:06:07,119
After it: a second way.

136
00:06:08,191 --> 00:06:11,457
Two separate points,
pointing the same direction.

137
00:06:11,477 --> 00:06:12,583
That's addition.

138
00:06:13,013 --> 00:06:15,405
The answer is B, additionally.

139
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:16,823
For this reason is the trap.

140
00:06:16,843 --> 00:06:19,358
Being above sea level
doesn't cause the permafrost.

141
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:22,271
Two facts side by side
aren't cause and effect.

142
00:06:23,057 --> 00:06:24,823
And nonetheless would need a contrast,

143
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:25,716
which isn't there.

144
00:06:25,736 --> 00:06:28,215
Instead would mean one
protection replaces the other,

145
00:06:28,235 --> 00:06:29,736
but the vault has both.

146
00:06:29,805 --> 00:06:31,091
Question five.

147
00:06:31,484 --> 00:06:35,535
In nineteen twenty-eight, Alexander
Fleming noticed that a mold growing in one

148
00:06:35,555 --> 00:06:38,912
of his laboratory dishes had
killed the bacteria around it.

149
00:06:39,145 --> 00:06:43,651
blank in nineteen forty, a team at
the University of Oxford showed that a

150
00:06:43,671 --> 00:06:46,473
purified form of the
substance the mold produced,

151
00:06:46,493 --> 00:06:50,350
penicillin, could protect mice
from a deadly bacterial infection.

152
00:06:50,404 --> 00:06:51,512
Pause and try it.

153
00:06:54,741 --> 00:06:56,170
The dates are your clue.

154
00:06:56,634 --> 00:06:59,206
Nineteen twenty-eight,
then nineteen forty.

155
00:06:59,849 --> 00:07:02,435
One event happened, and
then, twelve years on,

156
00:07:02,455 --> 00:07:03,634
another one did.

157
00:07:04,098 --> 00:07:05,277
That's sequence.

158
00:07:05,384 --> 00:07:07,991
The answer is A, later.

159
00:07:08,078 --> 00:07:12,935
Instead would mean the Oxford
work replaced Fleming's discovery.

160
00:07:14,328 --> 00:07:15,451
It built on it.

161
00:07:15,471 --> 00:07:18,272
The experiment isn't an
example of his observation,

162
00:07:18,292 --> 00:07:20,201
and it isn't a restatement either.

163
00:07:20,221 --> 00:07:21,614
It's a new event.

164
00:07:21,644 --> 00:07:22,752
Now the traps.

165
00:07:23,430 --> 00:07:27,823
Trap one: two choices
that do the same job.

166
00:07:27,894 --> 00:07:31,160
If therefore and as a
result are both choices,

167
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:32,124
they mean the same thing.

168
00:07:32,144 --> 00:07:33,767
They can't both be the one right answer,

169
00:07:33,787 --> 00:07:35,252
so usually neither is.

170
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:38,336
Trap two: the however
versus therefore flip.

171
00:07:38,479 --> 00:07:39,657
They're opposites.

172
00:07:39,943 --> 00:07:42,872
Therefore says the next
idea is what you'd expect.

173
00:07:43,157 --> 00:07:46,193
However says it goes
against what you'd expect.

174
00:07:46,622 --> 00:07:51,407
If you're stuck between them, ask:
is the second sentence a surprise?

175
00:07:51,438 --> 00:07:55,704
Trap three: grabbing a contrast word
because you noticed a contrast somewhere in

176
00:07:55,724 --> 00:07:56,775
the passage.

177
00:07:56,795 --> 00:07:59,295
Only the relationship
across the blank counts.

178
00:07:59,376 --> 00:08:00,376
Question six.

179
00:08:00,483 --> 00:08:04,570
In nineteen thirty-five, cane toads were
brought to Australia to control beetles

180
00:08:04,590 --> 00:08:06,662
that were damaging sugarcane crops.

181
00:08:06,742 --> 00:08:10,170
blank the toads had no
noticeable effect on the beetles.

182
00:08:10,201 --> 00:08:11,308
Pause and try it.

183
00:08:15,538 --> 00:08:17,859
The toads were brought in
to control the beetles.

184
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,947
Then they had no noticeable effect.

185
00:08:19,967 --> 00:08:21,717
Is that what you'd expect?

186
00:08:21,931 --> 00:08:22,911
No.

187
00:08:22,931 --> 00:08:24,360
The plan failed.

188
00:08:24,466 --> 00:08:26,340
That's a surprise, so it's a contrast:

189
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:27,360
however.

190
00:08:27,538 --> 00:08:29,217
The answer is C.

191
00:08:29,251 --> 00:08:30,751
Now look at A and B.

192
00:08:31,821 --> 00:08:34,124
Therefore and as a result do the same job,

193
00:08:34,144 --> 00:08:36,231
so they can't both be right.

194
00:08:36,251 --> 00:08:38,822
And they'd both say the
plan caused the failure,

195
00:08:39,822 --> 00:08:40,874
which makes no sense.

196
00:08:40,894 --> 00:08:42,787
For example doesn't fit either.

197
00:08:42,815 --> 00:08:43,886
Here's the flip.

198
00:08:44,601 --> 00:08:48,172
If the first sentence had said the
toads couldn't reach the beetles,

199
00:08:48,351 --> 00:08:49,886
then therefore would work.

200
00:08:51,029 --> 00:08:53,295
The words around the blank
decide the transition,

201
00:08:53,315 --> 00:08:54,386
not the topic.

202
00:08:54,458 --> 00:08:58,744
Last one, and it's harder.

203
00:08:59,815 --> 00:09:02,616
The first telegraph cable laid
across the Atlantic Ocean,

204
00:09:02,636 --> 00:09:06,814
completed in eighteen fifty-eight, stopped
working after only about three weeks.

205
00:09:07,092 --> 00:09:11,358
blank the short-lived cable proved that
an undersea cable could carry messages

206
00:09:11,378 --> 00:09:13,235
between Europe and North America.

207
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,423
Pause and try it.

208
00:09:15,209 --> 00:09:16,816
Take a little longer on this one.

209
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,718
The cable failed fast.

210
00:09:23,075 --> 00:09:24,519
But it still proved the idea worked.

211
00:09:24,539 --> 00:09:28,984
The relationship is: despite that.

212
00:09:29,004 --> 00:09:30,897
So the answer is B, nevertheless.

213
00:09:30,969 --> 00:09:36,004
Here's why in contrast is wrong, even
though it's also a contrast word.

214
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:38,540
In contrast compares two different things,

215
00:09:38,897 --> 00:09:41,182
like two planets or two telescopes.

216
00:09:42,004 --> 00:09:45,719
This passage has only
one thing, the cable.

217
00:09:45,897 --> 00:09:47,504
There's nothing to compare it to.

218
00:09:47,529 --> 00:09:50,529
Consequently would mean the
failure caused the proof.

219
00:09:51,386 --> 00:09:53,616
And nothing here is an example.

220
00:09:53,636 --> 00:09:56,187
So the rule from earlier
needs one adjustment.

221
00:09:56,207 --> 00:09:58,136
True synonyms are both out.

222
00:09:58,422 --> 00:10:02,029
But two words from the same family
can still do different jobs.

223
00:10:02,117 --> 00:10:04,239
Here's the method on one card.

224
00:10:04,259 --> 00:10:05,545
Cover the choices.

225
00:10:05,616 --> 00:10:08,295
Read the sentence before
and after the blank.

226
00:10:08,617 --> 00:10:10,275
Name the relationship.

227
00:10:10,295 --> 00:10:12,612
Then match the group, and read it back in.

228
00:10:12,632 --> 00:10:16,489
If you're stuck between two
choices, ask the sharper question.

229
00:10:16,775 --> 00:10:20,024
Is the second idea
expected, or a surprise?

230
00:10:20,345 --> 00:10:24,382
Are two things being compared, or
is one idea true despite another?

231
00:10:24,846 --> 00:10:26,331
That usually breaks the tie.

232
00:10:26,351 --> 00:10:27,351
Recap.

233
00:10:27,601 --> 00:10:30,458
Transitions test
relationships, not vocabulary.

234
00:10:30,530 --> 00:10:33,601
Predict the relationship
first, then find it.

235
00:10:33,673 --> 00:10:37,831
Watch for same-job pairs, the
however versus therefore flip,

236
00:10:37,851 --> 00:10:39,887
and contrast versus concession.

237
00:10:39,923 --> 00:10:43,331
For more practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter for

238
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,737
transitions under Expression of Ideas.

239
00:10:45,757 --> 00:10:48,665
All the questions in this video
were written for this video,

240
00:10:48,685 --> 00:10:50,329
in the style of the real test.

241
00:10:50,614 --> 00:10:52,293
If this helped, subscribe.

242
00:10:52,543 --> 00:10:55,721
Next up: command of evidence
questions with tables and graphs.
